{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q3646769","formula":"Cu₄Tl₂Se₄","hill":"Cu4Se4Tl2","elements":["Cu","Se","Tl"],"composition":{"Cu":4.0,"Se":4.0,"Tl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Bukovite","uk":"Буковіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Bukovite is a rare selenide mineral with formula Tl2Cu3FeSe4. It is a brown to black metallic mineral which crystallizes in the tetragonal system. It was first described in 1971 for an occurrence in the Bukov uranium mine, Rožná deposit, Vysočina Region, Moravia, Czech Republic.","uk":"Буковит — рідкісний мінерал, селенід з формулою Tl2Cu3FeSe4. Мінерал має металевий блиск, з кольором від коричневого до чорного, кристалізується в тетрагональній системі. Вперше він був описаний в 1971 році для прояву в урановому руднику «Буков», родовище Рожна, регіон Височина, Моравія, Чехія."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-5000","atoms":27,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.844,0.0,0.0],[0.0,3.844,0.0],[0.0,0.0,14.316]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Tl"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":14.316,"el":"Tl"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.844,"z":0.0,"el":"Tl"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.844,"z":14.316,"el":"Tl"},{"x":3.844,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Tl"},{"x":3.844,"y":0.0,"z":14.316,"el":"Tl"},{"x":3.844,"y":3.844,"z":0.0,"el":"Tl"},{"x":3.844,"y":3.844,"z":14.316,"el":"Tl"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.922,"z":3.579,"el":"Cu"},{"x":3.844,"y":1.922,"z":3.579,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.922,"y":0.0,"z":3.579,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.922,"y":3.844,"z":3.579,"el":"Cu"},{"x":1.922,"y":1.922,"z":2.058,"el":"Se"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":5.1,"el":"Se"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.844,"z":5.1,"el":"Se"},{"x":3.844,"y":0.0,"z":5.1,"el":"Se"},{"x":3.844,"y":3.844,"z":5.1,"el":"Se"},{"x":1.922,"y":1.922,"z":7.158,"el":"Tl"},{"x":1.922,"y":0.0,"z":10.737,"el":